  "texts": {
    "preamble": "The Food Inspector vs Mohd. Moizuddin on 26 June, 2023 The Honourable Sri Justice K.Surender Criminal Appeal No.471 of 2023 Judgment:",
    "facts": "It is case of Food Inspector that samples of Lehar 7-Up, Lehar Carbonated Water and Pepsi Cola were drawn and sent them for the purpose of analysis. The Public Analyst opined that the samples are 'adulterated'. Basing on the opinion of Public Analyst, the present complaint was filed by the Food Inspector against the accused for the offence under Section 16(1)(a)(i) for the Contravention of Section 2(ia)(m) and Section 7(i) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, vide C.C.No.17 of 2008. 4. Though the analysis report was received, there is a delay of two years in sending the analysis report and notice to the respondents - accused and the shelf life of the product is six months. Having found that the respondents - accused have lost their right to send the sample for Central Forensic Science Laboratory, Calcutta, the learned Magistrate has acquitted the respondents - accused.",
